      trivia: "The name El Güegüense derives from the protagonist of a masked drama born in Nicaragua under Spanish colonial rule: the “wise man” Güegüense, a cunning old man who bests his rulers with an artful forked tongue, and a symbol of Nicaraguan culture inscribed by UNESCO as intangible cultural heritage. Melillo's choice of the name for his debut was nothing less than a declaration of respect for Nicaraguan leaf tobacco and its culture. The spelling being hard to read, smokers often shorten it to “El G”. Note that “El Galan”, which appeared in the source material, is another company's brand, unconnected with Melillo."
